ck sea with a  privileged view on crimea reaches turkey  atipsa where it evolves into torque  stream 2 running up the continent up to  hungary the same applies to the blue  stream which crosses the black sea from  izobilny plant to reach ankara directly  the italian corridor is really  interesting especially for us italians  since we  rely on russian gas for about 40 percent  we are talking about the trans-adriatic  gas pipeline the t-a-p active since the  end of 2012 that will connect italy more  precisely the receiving terminal of  meladuno in napoleon straight to the  rich field of shahadanis in azerbaijan  on the coast of the caspian sea the tap  passes through albania and crosses greek  macedonia to kipoy on the turkish border  there it connects to tanap the  trans-anatolian pipeline all the way to  georgia where it finally attaches to the  south caucasian pipeline in 2021 seven  billion cubic meters passed through  maladuna but we're not done with russia  yet we need to talk about node stream  active since 2011 north stream creates a  direct supply line between wieberg in  russia and grieves world in germany  passing under the baltic sea attaching  to the grace of its wieberg pipeline  north stream supplies some of the gas  that passes through the northern lights  something like 55 billion cubic meters  per year can pass through north stream  although some european sanctions on gas  prom have reduced its actual capacity by  half what's the deal let's just build  another one right in september the  controversial project of nordstrom 2 was  completed an almost parallel pipeline  which instead of eborg it connects to us  luge and that would double the direct  supply capacity of germany from russia  with around 110 billion cubic meters if  all goes well and why should anything  ever go wrong well the list of views  against the nord stream 2 is quite long  and then we should also consider that  the nordstrom 2 company based in  switzerland went bankrupt day before 